2d:T97e,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"HowTo","name":"How to set up AI API spend monitoring with TryTokka","description":"Connect providers, set Scout alerts, and get spend warnings after daily sync â€” setup takes under five minutes.","totalTime":"PT5M","tool":[{"@type":"HowToTool","name":"TryTokka account"}],"step":[{"@type":"HowToStep","position":1,"name":"Create your free account","text":"Sign up with email or Google/GitHub. No credit card required for the 7-day trial. Go to Sign up and choose email or social login. You land in the setup wizard automatically â€” Scout walks you through the rest. Your workspace is created within seconds. Solo plan includes a full-featured trial.","url":"https://trytokka.com/signup"},{"@type":"HowToStep","position":2,"name":"Connect your first AI provider","text":"Paste an API key from OpenAI, Anthropic, Gemini, or OpenRouter. Keys are encrypted before they touch our database. Pick a provider in the setup wizard (or Connections in the sidebar). Follow the step-by-step instructions to find your key in the provider dashboard. Optional: add a project tag like \"Main app\" to split spend later. TryTokka syncs usage on first connection â€” your dashboard populates within seconds. After that, Scout syncs automatically once a day.","url":"https://trytokka.com/security"},{"@type":"HowToStep","position":3,"name":"Set a spend alert","text":"Choose a daily or monthly dollar limit. Scout emails after the next sync when you cross it â€” usually within ~24h (or Sync now). During setup, enter a threshold (e.g. $50/month). Pick daily or monthly â€” most indie devs start with monthly. Confirm your email. You get one alert per account â€” change its limit or period anytime under Alerts, and saving replaces the old one.","url":"https://trytokka.com/guide"},{"@type":"HowToStep","position":4,"name":"Then forget about it","text":"Scout syncs daily and emails you when spend crosses the limit you set. A 20-second glance makes alerts smarter â€” but you don't have to watch the meters yourself. Scout runs the daily sync and briefing automatically â€” you don't have to open anything. You only hear from Scout when spend crosses your limit or a spike appears. Want a live number? Open the dashboard and hit Sync now anytime â€” but you never have to. Use âŒ˜K (Ctrl+K) to jump to Connections, Alerts, or the full guide when you do drop in.","url":"https://trytokka.com/dashboard"}]}2e:T1f07,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Do I need a credit card to try TryTokka?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. The 7-day trial is full access with no card required."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Which providers are supported?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"OpenAI, Anthropic, Google Gemini, and OpenRouter are live-verified. Azure OpenAI, AWS Bedrock, and Cursor Teams connectors ship in-product and keep improving against live accounts. For flat monthly subscriptions like Cursor Pro or ChatGPT Plus, use manual entry."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can Scout tell me which AI models are costing me the most, and what to switch to?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. Based on your actual usage across the last 30 days, Scout estimates how much you'd save by switching to a cheaper model â€” shown in real dollars, not vague percentages. For example: \"Switch gpt-4o to gpt-4o-mini and save $44/month.\" These are estimates based on your token volume. Always test a sample before switching production traffic."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"I saw a spike in my spend. How do I know what caused it?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Go to Spend Analysis, click the spike day, and hit \"What caused this?\" â€” Scout shows a breakdown by model with what each model cost that day versus its rolling 7-day average, so you can see which model drove the spike and by how much."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can my team see the same dashboard?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes â€” upgrade to Team, invite members by email, and everyone gets read-only visibility."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What if I skip the setup wizard?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Go to Connections to add a provider anytime, or press âŒ˜K and search \"Setup wizard\"."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I install TryTokka as an app?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. Add it to your home screen on iPhone (Safari), Android (Chrome), or desktop (Chrome/Edge). You get the full dashboard in its own window, plus an optional spend badge on the icon."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the widget token for?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"It is a read-only key that lets the Chrome extension, home-screen badge, or your own scripts fetch month-to-date spend via /api/widget-summary â€” without your login session. Create and copy it under Settings â†’ Apps \u0026 widget."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How do I track OpenAI, Anthropic, and Gemini costs in one dashboard?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Connect each provider with a read-only billing key in the setup wizard. TryTokka pulls usage from all of them into a single dashboard, so you stop tabbing between separate billing pages."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How do I get alerted before my AI API bill gets too high?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Set a daily or monthly dollar limit during setup. Scout checks after each sync (once daily automatically, or when you click Sync now) and emails you â€” usually within ~24h of crossing the limit. Not a real-time circuit breaker."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is there a free way to track AI API spend?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. Start with a 7-day free trial (full access, no card). After that you can stay on Free forever â€” one provider, the dashboard, and a monthly summary email â€” or upgrade to Solo from $9/month for multi-provider alerts and spike tools."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Do I need an API key to use TryTokka?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes â€” TryTokka reads provider billing/usage reports with a read-only billing or Admin key (not a proxy in your request path). OpenAI needs an org Admin key (sk-admin-â€¦), not a project sk- key. Anthropic, Gemini, and others use their documented billing credentials. You can revoke a connection anytime."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What type of API key do I need for OpenAI?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"An Admin / organization API key (starts with sk-admin-...), not a project or user key (sk-...), because usage figures are only readable with an admin credential. Create one at platform.openai.com â†’ Settings â†’ Organization â†’ Admin keys, and set Permissions to Read only. That matters: an admin key with full permissions can manage projects, members and other keys, whereas a read-only one can do nothing but read â€” which is all TryTokka needs for the single usage endpoint it calls. Other providers (Anthropic, Gemini, OpenRouter, Azure, Bedrock, Cursor) use their standard API or billing keys."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is TryTokka a subscription limit tracker for Claude or ChatGPT chats?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. TryTokka monitors API and org billing spend across providers (keys you connect), with daily Scout threshold emails. It is not a menu-bar widget for chat-plan session windows (5-hour / weekly consumer caps). If you need invoice-level API cost truth for builders and teams, you are in the right place."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Why not just check each provider's free billing dashboard?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Those dashboards are reactive â€” they show what you already spent. Scout is proactive and emails you before you hit your limit. And checking three separate logins is a habit that quietly stops happening after a few days; one dashboard is the one that sticks."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How is TryTokka different from a proxy tool like Helicone?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"A proxy sits between your app and the AI provider, so every prompt and response routes through it and you have to change your API base URL in each project. TryTokka only reads your provider billing totals â€” no code changes, no proxy in your request path, and your prompts never leave the provider."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is TryTokka related to TikTok?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. TryTokka (trytokka.com) is an AI API spend monitoring dashboard for developers â€” it tracks eight API providers plus flat subscriptions, with daily Scout threshold alerts. It has no affiliation with TikTok, ByteDance, or any social media / short-video app. It is also not ToreTokka (toretokka.com / à¦Ÿà¦°à§‡à¦Ÿà¦•à§à¦•à¦¾), a Bangladeshi news-aggregator app, not Tokka, the stranger video-chat app on Google Play and the App Store, and not Tokka Labs (tokkalabs.com), a crypto proprietary-trading firm. Searches for Tryakka, tryakka, or â€œtry tokkaâ€ are the same product; those are misspellings of TryTokka, not a different app. A search for trytokka means this spend dashboard."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is TryTokka the same as ToreTokka?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. TryTokka at trytokka.com is an AI API spend dashboard for developers (Scout threshold emails after daily sync). ToreTokka at toretokka.com is a news-aggregator app in Bangladesh (à¦Ÿà¦°à§‡à¦Ÿà¦•à§à¦•à¦¾). They are unrelated. If Google or an AI Overview shows ToreTokka for the query trytokka, that is the wrong product â€” this site is the spend monitor."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is TryTokka the Tokka video chat app?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. TryTokka at trytokka.com monitors AI API spend. Tokka on Google Play and the App Store is a stranger video-chat app. They are unrelated. A search for trytokka means this spend dashboard."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is TryTokka a crypto platform or Tokka Labs?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. TryTokka at trytokka.com is an AI API spend dashboard for developers. It has no cryptocurrency wallets, trading tools, or market news. Tokka Labs (tokkalabs.com) is an unrelated Singapore crypto proprietary-trading firm. A search for trytokka means this spend dashboard."}}]}22:[[["$","script","jsonld-0",{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"$2d"}}],["$","script","jsonld-1",{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"$2e"}}],"$L2f","$L30"],"$L31"]
